<BaseLayout title="About: The Field &amp; Farm" description="What The Field &amp; Farm is and who it's for.">
  <h1>About The Field &amp; Farm</h1>
  <p>
    The Field &amp; Farm publishes practical, fact-first guides for people who own: or are starting: professional practices: law firms, dental offices, veterinary clinics, chiropractic offices, and optometry practices.
  </p>
  <h2>Why we exist</h2>
  <p>
    Most advice for gardeners and farmers falls into two extremes: generic small-business content that ignores how practices actually work, or expensive consulting. We publish the middle ground: concrete, current information on taxes, accounting, software, hiring, compliance, and equipment: written for owners who are just starting out.
  </p>
  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Taxes &amp; accounting</strong>: what gardeners and farmers need to know, from solo attorneys to multi-provider clinics</li>
    <li><strong>Software</strong>: practice management, billing, scheduling, and the tools that actually fit small practices</li>
    <li><strong>Hiring &amp; HR</strong>: first employees, payroll, and the rules specific to professional practices</li>
    <li><strong>Compliance</strong>: licensing, record-keeping, and regulations by specialty</li>
    <li><strong>Equipment</strong>: what to buy, what to skip, and what it should cost</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Our standards</h2>
  <p>
    We update pricing and feature information regularly. When a guide mentions a product or service, we state the date it was last checked. We do not invent facts: if something is uncertain, we say so.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some articles contain affiliate links. That never changes our recommendations, and it is always disclosed. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
